WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.088
Start with why.

2
00:00:01.088 --> 00:00:05.384
Most federal estates still run
the client/server model they built

3
00:00:05.384 --> 00:00:09.525
in the early 2000s, with an Active
Directory forest at the center.

4
00:00:09.525 --> 00:00:13.671
Since Windows 2000, the organizational
unit has grouped objects

5
00:00:13.671 --> 00:00:17.587
for delegating administrative
rights and assigning policy.

6
00:00:17.587 --> 00:00:20.686
So placing a user or a
computer in the tree decided,

7
00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:24.769
at the same moment and with no
separate record, who administers it,

8
00:00:24.769 --> 00:00:28.548
which Group Policy applies to
it, what its groups let it reach,

9
00:00:28.548 --> 00:00:33.462
how it's named in directory-integrated
DNS, and which certificates it receives.

10
00:00:33.462 --> 00:00:36.394
It was efficient, and for
a quarter century agencies

11
00:00:36.394 --> 00:00:39.462
got governance as a side
effect of running a directory.

12
00:00:39.462 --> 00:00:41.562
The cost is that it was never stated.

13
00:00:41.562 --> 00:00:43.700
The cloud estate doesn't inherit it.

14
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.062
Entra ID's administrative
units can't be nested.

15
00:00:47.062 --> 00:00:51.448
Intune applies policy to groups
with no hierarchy, and two policies

16
00:00:51.448 --> 00:00:55.912
that disagree produce a conflict to
resolve, not an inheritance rule.

17
00:00:55.912 --> 00:01:02.613
Access, names and trust move to Conditional
Access, a DDI platform and a target PKI.

18
00:01:02.613 --> 00:01:06.199
Each replacement needs someone to
decide what the old placement meant.

19
00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:09.680
An agency that moves users
and retires the forest without

20
00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.450
recovering those decisions
doesn't modernize its governance.

21
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:14.500
It deletes it.

22
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:18.437
So the first decision is the
sponsor's, when the charter is signed:

23
00:01:18.437 --> 00:01:23.637
treat modernization as governance
reconstruction, not only a technical migration.

24
00:01:23.637 --> 00:01:26.983
If stakeholders don't accept
that, the charter says,

25
00:01:26.983 --> 00:01:29.900
resistance becomes the
program's main risk.
